    1. Introduction
      1.1    Problem Background
     The illegal wildlife trade not only causes enormous damage to the environment, but also
poses a serious threat to global biodiversity. The trade is estimated to involve as much as
$26.5 billion annually, making it the fourth largest illegal trade globally. However, global
efforts to address the problem still face significant challenges.




                                                           型
     We are therefore proposing a data-driven, five-year program aimed at significantly
reducing the illegal wildlife trade through accurate client and program selection.




