      4.2        Selection of evaluation indicators
     To model client evaluation, we chose power, resources, interest, and influence as first-
            信




level indicators.
     Power: Power includes the ability to enforce laws as well as to strategy, allocate
  微




resources, and set industry standards. Clients with decision-making and strategy
policymaking power can directly influence laws and regulations, and implement stronger
regulatory measures to effectively combat illegal wildlife trade.
     Resources: Funding is the foundation for effective programs. Adequate funding can be
used to support enforcement activities, public awareness and conservation programs.
Adequate financial resources not only ensure the sustainability of the program, but also

                                                                                                2
