        6.3.2 Strantge III: Reducing illegal trade sales
     In the FIWT model, the parameters v and r are affected by a number of factors. Both of
                                                       ：
them will increase after enhanced intervention. Some of the specific interventions are
described below.




                                                      els
     (1) Cracking down on illegal markets and increasing regulation. Wildlife markets are
                             号
vulnerable to infiltration by criminals. Therefore, there is a need to combat illegal trading
networks and sales channels. This requires the Government to strengthen the authentication


                                                    od
and certification mechanisms for legal sales to prevent illegal products from entering the
                            众


market.
                                                  Hm
     (2) Use of advanced technical equipment and strengthening of customs inspections:
Customs should strengthen inspections of imported and exported goods, especially more
                   公



stringent scrutiny of goods involving wild animals and their products. For example, X-ray
scanners are used to better identify and detect wild animals and their products hidden in cargo.
     (3) Establishing transnational co-operation: between 1999 and 2018, nearly 6,000
                                               AT
          信




species have been seized and suspected smugglers of more than 150 nationalities have been
identified. This shows that wildlife crime is indeed a global problem. Therefore, countries
should enhance intelligence sharing and develop common action plans to combat
微

                                       M



transnational illegal wildlife trade.
